schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Quadratic funding
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A matching-fund mechanism that weights the number of backers more
    heavily than the size of any single gift, so broad community support
    outweighs one large donor ("one whale").
  source_traditions:
    - Gitcoin Grants matching-round design
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Explains why Gitcoin Grants is recommended as the main funding on-ramp
    for a local node once it has a track record — small, broad-based
    community donations get amplified by a matching pool.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - gitcoin-grants
    - gitcoin-passport
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      quadratic-funding-vs-flat-matching — rewards breadth of small backers
      rather than simply matching whatever is donated 1:1
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    The article doesn't cover known quadratic-funding attack vectors (e.g.
    collusion/Sybil attacks), which Gitcoin Passport is partly designed to
    mitigate — worth linking if a dedicated quadratic-funding page exists.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/first-90-days.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
